# NET88 Design System - Text Utilities

## Overview
Text utilities cung cấp các utility classes để style text nhanh chóng mà không cần viết custom CSS. Các classes này cover alignment, decoration, transform, wrapping, và nhiều thuộc tính text khác.

---

## Text Alignment

### Horizontal Alignment
```scss
.text-left { text-align: left; }
.text-center { text-align: center; }
.text-right { text-align: right; }
.text-justify { text-align: justify; }
```

**Usage:**
```vue
<p class="text-left">Left aligned text</p>
<p class="text-center">Center aligned text</p>
<p class="text-right">Right aligned text</p>
<p class="text-justify">Justified text that spreads evenly across the line</p>
```

---

## Text Decoration

### Underline, Line-through, None
```scss
.text-underline { text-decoration: underline; }
.text-line-through { text-decoration: line-through; }
.text-no-underline { text-decoration: none; }
```

**Usage:**
```vue
<p class="text-underline">Underlined text</p>
<p class="text-line-through">Strikethrough text</p>
<a href="#" class="text-no-underline">Link without underline</a>
```

---

## Text Transform

### Case Transformation
```scss
.text-uppercase { text-transform: uppercase; }
.text-lowercase { text-transform: lowercase; }
.text-capitalize { text-transform: capitalize; }
```

**Usage:**
```vue
<p class="text-uppercase">UPPERCASE TEXT</p>
<p class="text-lowercase">lowercase text</p>
<p class="text-capitalize">Capitalized Text</p>
```

---

## Text Overflow

### Truncation
```scss
.text-truncate {
  overflow: hidden;
  text-overflow: ellipsis;
  white-space: nowrap;
}
```

**Usage:**
```vue
<div class="text-truncate" style="max-width: 200px;">
  This is a very long text that will be truncated with an ellipsis
</div>
```

### Multi-line Truncation
```scss
.text-truncate-2 {
  display: -webkit-box;
  -webkit-line-clamp: 2;
  -webkit-box-orient: vertical;
  overflow: hidden;
}

.text-truncate-3 {
  display: -webkit-box;
  -webkit-line-clamp: 3;
  -webkit-box-orient: vertical;
  overflow: hidden;
}
```

**Usage:**
```vue
<p class="text-truncate-2">
  This is a long paragraph that will be truncated after 2 lines with an ellipsis.
  Additional text will be hidden and replaced with three dots.
</p>
```

---

## Text Wrapping

### Wrapping Control
```scss
.text-wrap { white-space: normal; }
.text-nowrap { white-space: nowrap; }
.text-break { word-wrap: break-word; overflow-wrap: break-word; }
```

**Usage:**
```vue
<p class="text-wrap">Normal wrapping text</p>
<p class="text-nowrap">No wrapping text</p>
<p class="text-break">LongWordWithoutSpacesWillBreak</p>
```

---

## Letter Spacing

### Spacing Scale
```scss
.tracking-tighter { letter-spacing: -0.05em; }
.tracking-tight { letter-spacing: -0.025em; }
.tracking-normal { letter-spacing: 0; }
.tracking-wide { letter-spacing: 0.025em; }
.tracking-wider { letter-spacing: 0.05em; }
.tracking-widest { letter-spacing: 0.1em; }
```

**Usage:**
```vue
<p class="tracking-tighter">Tighter letter spacing</p>
<p class="tracking-normal">Normal letter spacing</p>
<p class="tracking-widest">Widest letter spacing</p>
```

---

## Word Spacing

### Word Spacing Scale
```scss
.word-spacing-tight { word-spacing: -0.05em; }
.word-spacing-normal { word-spacing: normal; }
.word-spacing-wide { word-spacing: 0.1em; }
.word-spacing-wider { word-spacing: 0.2em; }
```

**Usage:**
```vue
<p class="word-spacing-tight">Tight word spacing</p>
<p class="word-spacing-normal">Normal word spacing</p>
<p class="word-spacing-wider">Wider word spacing</p>
```

---

## Line Height

### Line Height Scale
```scss
.leading-none { line-height: 1; }
.leading-tight { line-height: 1.25; }
.leading-snug { line-height: 1.375; }
.leading-normal { line-height: 1.5; }
.leading-relaxed { line-height: 1.625; }
.leading-loose { line-height: 2; }
```

**Usage:**
```vue
<p class="leading-tight">Tight line height</p>
<p class="leading-normal">Normal line height</p>
<p class="leading-loose">Loose line height</p>
```

---

## Text Indent

### Indentation
```scss
.text-indent { text-indent: 2em; }
.text-indent-lg { text-indent: 4em; }
```

**Usage:**
```vue
<p class="text-indent">
  This paragraph has a text indent of 2em. The first line will be indented.
</p>
```

---

## Font Style

### Normal vs Italic
```scss
.text-italic { font-style: italic; }
.text-not-italic { font-style: normal; }
```

**Usage:**
```vue
<p class="text-italic">Italic text</p>
<p class="text-not-italic">Normal text</p>
```

---

## Font Variant

### Small Caps
```scss
.text-small-caps { font-variant: small-caps; }
```

**Usage:**
```vue
<p class="text-small-caps">Small Caps Text</p>
```

---

## Text Selection

### Selection Color
```scss
::selection {
  background-color: $net88-primary;
  color: white;
}
```

**Usage:**
```scss
// Applied globally via main.scss
// User selection will be highlighted with primary color
```

---

## User Select

### Selection Control
```scss
.select-all { user-select: all; }
.select-auto { user-select: auto; }
.select-none { user-select: none; }
.select-text { user-select: text; }
```

**Usage:**
```vue
<p class="select-all">Click to select all text</p>
<p class="select-none">Text cannot be selected</p>
```

---

## Writing Mode

### Horizontal vs Vertical
```scss
.writing-horizontal { writing-mode: horizontal-tb; }
.writing-vertical { writing-mode: vertical-rl; }
```

**Usage:**
```vue
<p class="writing-horizontal">Horizontal text</p>
<p class="writing-vertical">Vertical text</p>
```

---

## Text Orientation

### Orientation Control
```scss
.text-orientation-mixed { text-orientation: mixed; }
.text-orientation-upright { text-orientation: upright; }
```

**Usage:**
```vue
<p class="writing-vertical text-orientation-upright">
  Vertical upright text
</p>
```

---

## Direction

### Text Direction
```scss
.text-ltr { direction: ltr; }
.text-rtl { direction: rtl; }
```

**Usage:**
```vue
<p class="text-ltr">Left to right text</p>
<p class="text-rtl">טקסט מימין לשמאל</p>
```

---

## CSS Implementation

```scss
// Text Alignment
.text-left { text-align: left; }
.text-center { text-align: center; }
.text-right { text-align: right; }
.text-justify { text-align: justify; }

// Text Decoration
.text-underline { text-decoration: underline; }
.text-line-through { text-decoration: line-through; }
.text-no-underline { text-decoration: none; }

// Text Transform
.text-uppercase { text-transform: uppercase; }
.text-lowercase { text-transform: lowercase; }
.text-capitalize { text-transform: capitalize; }

// Text Overflow
.text-truncate {
  overflow: hidden;
  text-overflow: ellipsis;
  white-space: nowrap;
}

.text-truncate-2 {
  display: -webkit-box;
  -webkit-line-clamp: 2;
  -webkit-box-orient: vertical;
  overflow: hidden;
}

.text-truncate-3 {
  display: -webkit-box;
  -webkit-line-clamp: 3;
  -webkit-box-orient: vertical;
  overflow: hidden;
}

// Text Wrapping
.text-wrap { white-space: normal; }
.text-nowrap { white-space: nowrap; }
.text-break { word-wrap: break-word; overflow-wrap: break-word; }

// Letter Spacing
.tracking-tighter { letter-spacing: -0.05em; }
.tracking-tight { letter-spacing: -0.025em; }
.tracking-normal { letter-spacing: 0; }
.tracking-wide { letter-spacing: 0.025em; }
.tracking-wider { letter-spacing: 0.05em; }
.tracking-widest { letter-spacing: 0.1em; }

// Word Spacing
.word-spacing-tight { word-spacing: -0.05em; }
.word-spacing-normal { word-spacing: normal; }
.word-spacing-wide { word-spacing: 0.1em; }
.word-spacing-wider { word-spacing: 0.2em; }

// Line Height
.leading-none { line-height: 1; }
.leading-tight { line-height: 1.25; }
.leading-snug { line-height: 1.375; }
.leading-normal { line-height: 1.5; }
.leading-relaxed { line-height: 1.625; }
.leading-loose { line-height: 2; }

// Text Indent
.text-indent { text-indent: 2em; }
.text-indent-lg { text-indent: 4em; }

// Font Style
.text-italic { font-style: italic; }
.text-not-italic { font-style: normal; }

// Font Variant
.text-small-caps { font-variant: small-caps; }

// Text Selection
::selection {
  background-color: $net88-primary;
  color: white;
}

// User Select
.select-all { user-select: all; }
.select-auto { user-select: auto; }
.select-none { user-select: none; }
.select-text { user-select: text; }

// Writing Mode
.writing-horizontal { writing-mode: horizontal-tb; }
.writing-vertical { writing-mode: vertical-rl; }

// Text Orientation
.text-orientation-mixed { text-orientation: mixed; }
.text-orientation-upright { text-orientation: upright; }

// Direction
.text-ltr { direction: ltr; }
.text-rtl { direction: rtl; }
```

---

## Dark Mode Support

```scss
.dark-mode {
  ::selection {
    background-color: $net88-primary-light;
    color: $net88-gray-900;
  }
}
```

---

## Responsive Text Utilities

```scss
.text-responsive {
  font-size: $net88-font-size-sm; // 14px on mobile

  @media (min-width: 768px) {
    font-size: $net88-font-size-base; // 16px on tablet
  }

  @media (min-width: 1024px) {
    font-size: $net88-font-size-lg; // 18px on desktop
  }
}
```

---

## Usage Examples

### Truncated Card Title
```vue
<Card variant="default" padding="md">
  <h3 class="text-truncate" style="max-width: 250px;">
    This is a very long card title that will be truncated
  </h3>
  <p class="text-muted">Card content...</p>
</Card>
```

### Multi-line Description
```vue
<div class="text-truncate-3" style="max-width: 300px;">
  This is a long description that will be truncated after 3 lines.
  Any additional text will be hidden and replaced with an ellipsis.
  This helps maintain consistent layout heights across cards.
</div>
```

### Call to Action
```vue
<div class="text-center">
  <h2 class="text-uppercase tracking-wide">Limited Time Offer</h2>
  <p class="text-italic text-muted">Don't miss out!</p>
</div>
```

### Code Block
```vue
<code class="text-nowrap font-mono">
  const example = "This code won't wrap";
</code>
```

---

## Best Practices

### DO ✅
- Use `text-truncate` for consistent layout heights
- Use `tracking-wide` for uppercase headings
- Use `leading-relaxed` for long-form content
- Use `text-break` for URLs or long words
- Ensure text remains readable in dark mode

### DON'T ❌
- Don't use `text-nowrap` on long paragraphs
- Don't use `tracking-widest` on body text
- Don't use `text-uppercase` on long passages
- Don't override these utilities with inline styles unnecessarily
- Don't use `select-none` on interactive elements

---

## Accessibility

- ✅ Text truncation should have full text available on hover/focus
- ✅ Letter spacing adjustments maintain readability
- ✅ Line height should be at least 1.5 for body text
- ✅ Text color contrast meets WCAG AA standards
- ✅ RTL languages supported with direction utilities

---

## Browser Support

All text utilities are supported in:
- ✅ Chrome 90+
- ✅ Firefox 88+
- ✅ Safari 14+
- ✅ Edge 90+

**Note:** `-webkit-line-clamp` for multi-line truncation is widely supported in modern browsers.

