## Best Practices

### DO ✅
- Use semantic colors for status backgrounds (success, error, warning)
- Ensure text contrast on all backgrounds
- Use gradients sparingly for emphasis
- Use patterns for decorative backgrounds only
- Test backgrounds in both light and dark modes

### DON'T ❌
- Don't use gradients that reduce readability
- Don't use busy patterns behind text
- Don't use light text on light backgrounds
- Don't use background images without fallback colors
- Don't use fixed backgrounds on mobile (performance issue)

---

## Accessibility

- ✅ Background color contrast with text meets WCAG AA (4.5:1)
- ✅ Gradients maintain contrast throughout
- ✅ Patterns are subtle and don't interfere with readability
- ✅ High contrast mode supported
- ✅ Reduced motion preferences respected

---

## Performance Tips

- Use CSS gradients instead of image gradients when possible
- Optimize background images (compress, use WebP)
- Use `bg-fixed` sparingly on mobile (performance impact)
- Consider using solid colors instead of patterns for better performance
- Use `will-change` property carefully with animated backgrounds

